<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aegidius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">?–464/465</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aegidius was a Roman general who commanded in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> from about 457 until his death in 464 or 465. Appointed by Emperor Majorian, he refused to accept Majorian's murder in 461 and ruled the region around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soissons">Soissons</a> independently of the Italian court, defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> in 463. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syagrius">Syagrius</a> inherited his power in what historians call the Domain of Soissons.</p></div>
